<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hammuda Pasha Bey</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1666</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Hammuda ibn Murad</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hammuda Pasha Bey was the second bey of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muradid-dynasty">Muradid dynasty</a> of Ottoman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tunisia">Tunisia</a>, ruling from 1631 to 1666. Son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/murad-i">Murad I</a> Bey, he received the title of pasha from the Ottoman sultan and made the office of bey hereditary in his family, overshadowing the dey. He extended control over the interior tribes and built mosques and other works in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tunis">Tunis</a>.</p></div>
